   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `functionTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `functionTypeIR`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `functionTypeIR'` matches pattern `FUNCTION ( % ) -> %`.
  ... Let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `functionTypeIR'`.
  ... Group function: `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `functionTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `functionTypeIR`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `functionTypeIR'` matches pattern `ACTION ( % )`.
  ... Let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `functionTypeIR'`.
  ... Group action: `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~ )` and `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~ )`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `functionTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `functionTypeIR`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `functionTypeIR'` matches pattern `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( % ) -> %`.
  ... Let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `functionTypeIR'`.
  ... Group externfunction: `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if `routineTypeIR` has type `methodTypeIR`:
 .. Let `methodTypeIR` be `routineTypeIR`.
