  ... Let `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `methodTypeIR'`.
  ... Group builtinmethod: `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `methodTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `routineTypeIR'` has type `methodTypeIR`.
  ... Let `methodTypeIR'` be `routineTypeIR'`.
  ... Check that `methodTypeIR'` matches pattern `EXTERN_METHOD ( % ) -> %`.
  ... Let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~` be `methodTypeIR'`.
  ... Group externmethod: `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` and `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~ ) -> typeIR~ret_b~`

   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for each `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~ret_a~` and `typeIR~ret_b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret_a~` be `methodTypeIR`:
