relation RoutineTypeDef_alpha: `routineTypeDefIR` and `routineTypeDefIR'`

. If `routineTypeDefIR` has type `routineTypeIR`:
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~a~` be `routineTypeDefIR`.
 .. Check that `routineTypeDefIR'` has type `routineTypeIR`.
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~b~` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group mono: `routineTypeIR~a~` and `routineTypeIR~b~`

  ... Check that <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a~` and `routineTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `routineTypeDefIR` has type `polyRoutineTypeDefIR`:
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~a~ < tid~a~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR`.
 .. Check that `routineTypeDefIR'` has type `polyRoutineTypeDefIR`.
 .. Let `routineTypeIR~b~ < tid~b~^{asterisk}^ , tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `routineTypeDefIR'`.
 .. Group poly: `routineTypeIR~a~ < tid~a~ , tid~hidden_a~ >` and `routineTypeIR~b~ < tid~b~ , tid~hidden_b~ >`

  ... Check that the length of `tid~a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that the length of `tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be `$fresh_tids(the length of tid~a~^{asterisk}^ + the length of tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `tid~a'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~a~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_a~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~a~` be `{ tid~a'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` be `$subst_routineType(theta~a~, routineTypeIR~a~)`.
  ... Let `tid~b'~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~b~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~hidden_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `theta~b~` be `{ tid~b'~ : TID tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` be `$subst_routineType(theta~b~, routineTypeIR~b~)`.
  ... Check that <<RoutineType_alpha, `routineTypeIR~a_subst~` and `routineTypeIR~b_subst~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.

relation Type_wf: `bound` and `typeIR'''`

. If `typeIR'''` has type `baseTypeIR`:
 .. Let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group baseTypeIR: `bound` and `baseTypeIR`

  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `nameTypeIR`:
 .. Let `TID tid` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group nameTypeIR: `bound` and `TID tid`

  ... Check that `$in_set<tid>(tid, bound)`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `specializedTypeIR`:
 .. Let `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group specializedTypeIR: `bound` and `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~ >`

  ... Let `typeIR` be `$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `typedefTypeIR`:
 .. Let `TYPEDEF _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group typedefTypeIR: `bound` and `TYPEDEF _ typeIR`

  ... Check that `$nestable_typedef(typeIR)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `newTypeIR`:
 .. Let `TYPE _ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group newTypeIR: `bound` and `TYPE _ typeIR`

  ... Check that `$nestable_new(typeIR)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `listTypeIR`:
 .. Let `LIST < typeIR >` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group listTypeIR: `bound` and `LIST < typeIR >`

  ... Check that `$nestable_list(typeIR)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `tupleTypeIR`:
 .. Let `TUPLE < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group tupleTypeIR: `bound` and `TUPLE < typeIR >`

  ... Check that `$nestable_tuple(typeIR)`, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `headerStackTypeIR`:
 .. Let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group headerStackTypeIR: `bound` and `typeIR [ _ ]`

  ... Check that `$nestable_headerStack(typeIR)`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `structTypeIR`:
 .. Let `STRUCT _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group structTypeIR: `bound` and `STRUCT _ { typeIR id ; }`

  ... Check that `$distinct_<id>(id^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Check that `$nestable_struct(typeIR)`, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `headerTypeIR`:
 .. Let `HEADER _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`.
 .. Group headerTypeIR: `bound` and `HEADER _ { typeIR id ; }`

  ... Check that `$distinct_<id>(id^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Check that `$nestable_header(typeIR)`, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds, for each `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR'''` has type `headerUnionTypeIR`:
 .. Let `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR id ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`.
