relation ParameterType_wf: `bound` and `direction typeIR _ value''^?^`

. Check that `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`.
. If `value''^?^` matches pattern `()`:
 .. Group default-empty-extern: `bound` and `typeIR _ ?()`

  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR>>)`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `?value` be `value''^?^`:
 .. Group default-some-extern: `bound` and `typeIR _ ?value`

  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR>>)`.
  ... The relation holds.
. If `value''^?^` matches pattern `()`:
 .. Group default-none-not-extern: `bound` and `direction typeIR _ ?()`

  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR>>)`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if let `?value` be `value''^?^`:
 .. Group default-some-not-extern: `bound` and `direction typeIR _ ?value`

  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR>>)`.
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
   .... The relation holds.

  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... The relation holds.

