 .. If `memberAccessBaseIR` matches pattern `TYPE %`:
  ... Let `TYPE prefixedNameIR` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type: `p`, `TC`, and `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR # ( typeIR~base~ _ )`

   .... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `enumTypeIR`.
   .... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM tid { id~member~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `id~member~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Result in `tid . nameIR`.

   .... Else if let `ENUM tid # typeIR { id~member~ = value~member~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `value'^?^` be `$assoc_<id, value>(nameIR, (id~member~, value~member~)^{asterisk}^)`.
    ..... Check that `value'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
    ..... Let `?value` be `value'^?^`.
    ..... Result in `tid . nameIR # value`.
 .. If `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
  ... Check that `nameIR` is equal to `"size"`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "size" # ( _ _ )`

   .... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
   .... Let `_ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR`.
   .... Result in `D n~size~`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `sliceAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ] # ( _ _ )`

  ... Let `value~base~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `$bitacc_op(value~base~, value~hi~, value~lo~)`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `callExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Check that `callExpressionIR` matches pattern `% < % > ( % )`.
 .. Let `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`.
 .. If `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size: `p`, `TC`, and `routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( [ ] ) # ( _ _ )`

   .... If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
    ..... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
    ..... Result in `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.

   .... Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
    ..... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
    ..... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
    ..... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
    ..... If `typeDefIR` has type `typeIR`:
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be `typeDefIR`.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.

    ..... Else if `typeDefIR` has type `polyTypeDefIR`:
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~ < tid^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`.
     ...... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
     ...... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.
 .. If `routineTargetIR` matches pattern `( % )`:
  ... Let `( routineTargetIR )` be `routineTargetIR`.
  ... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized: `p`, `TC`, and `( routineTargetIR ) < typeArgumentIR > ( argumentIR ) # ( typeIR ctk )`

   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) # ( _ _ )`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in `value`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `parenthesizedExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `( typedExpressionIR )` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `( typedExpressionIR ) # ( _ _ )`

  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `value`.

relation Type_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeOrVoid`

. Group primitiveType: `p`, `TC`, and `typeOrVoid`

 .. If `typeOrVoid` matches pattern `VOID`:
  ... Result in the type `VOID` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. If `BOOL` is equal to `typeOrVoid`:
  ... Result in the type `BOOL` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. If `ERROR` is equal to `typeOrVoid`:
  ... Result in the type `ERROR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. If `MATCH_KIND` is equal to `typeOrVoid`:
  ... Result in the type `MATCH_KIND` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. If `STRING` is equal to `typeOrVoid`:
  ... Result in the type `STRING` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. If `typeOrVoid` has type `baseType`:
 .. Let `baseType` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Check that `baseType` matches pattern `INT`.
 .. Group arbint: `p`, `TC`, and `INT`

  ... Result in the type `INT` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixint: `p`, `TC`, and `baseType`

  ... If let `INT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if let `INT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixbit: `p`, `TC`, and `baseType`

  ... If `baseType` matches pattern `BIT`:
   .... Result in the type `BIT < 1 >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if let `BIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if let `BIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group varbit: `p`, `TC`, and `baseType`

  ... If let `VARBIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if let `VARBIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

. Else if `typeOrVoid` has type `prefixedTypeName`:
 .. Let `prefixedTypeName` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Group prefixedTypeName: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedTypeName`

  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... If `typeDefIR` has type `typeIR`:
   .... Let `typeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if `typeDefIR` has type `polyTypeDefIR`:
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR < [ ] >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

. Else if `typeOrVoid` has type `specializedType`:
 .. Let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList' >` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Group specializedType: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList' >`

  ... If `typeArgumentList'` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
   .... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `typeIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... If `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`:
   .... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `polyTypeDefIR`.
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >` be `polyTypeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList')`.
   .... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p TC |- typeArgument^{asterisk}^ : typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ # tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.

. Else if `typeOrVoid` has type `headerStackType`:
 .. Let `namedType [ expression~size~ ]` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Group headerStackType: `p`, `TC`, and `namedType [ expression~size~ ]`

  ... If `namedType` has type `prefixedTypeName`:
   .... Let `prefixedTypeName` be `namedType`.
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `prefixedTypeName`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value~size~)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Let `typeIR~stack~` be `TID "T" [ n~size~ ]`.
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR~stack~` be `typeIR~stack~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~stack~ < [typeIR~base~] >` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.

  ... Else if `namedType` has type `specializedType`:
   .... Let `specializedType` be `namedType`.
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `specializedType`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value~size~)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Let `typeIR~stack~` be `TID "T" [ n~size~ ]`.
   .... Let `polyTypeDefIR~stack~` be `typeIR~stack~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
   .... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~stack~ < [typeIR~base~] >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.

. Else if `typeOrVoid` has type `listType`:
 .. Let `LIST < typeArgument >` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Group listType: `p`, `TC`, and `LIST < typeArgument >`

  ... <<TypeArgument_ok, `p TC |- typeArgument : typeIR~arg~ # tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~list~` be `LIST < TID "T" >`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR~list~` be `typeIR~list~ < ["T"] , [ ] >`.
  ... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~list~ < [typeIR~arg~] >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.

. Else if `typeOrVoid` has type `tupleType`:
 .. Let `TUPLE < typeArgumentList >` be `typeOrVoid`.
 .. Group tupleType: `p`, `TC`, and `TUPLE < typeArgumentList >`

  ... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)`.
  ... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p TC |- typeArgument^{asterisk}^ : typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ # tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `i~idx~^{asterisk}^` be `$init_(the length of typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~tparam~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~tparam~` be `"T" ++ $int_to_text(i~idx~)`
--
+
for each `i~idx~` in `i~idx~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~tuple~` be `TUPLE < TID tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^ >`.
  ... Let `polyTypeDefIR~tuple~` be `typeIR~tuple~ < tid~tparam~^{asterisk}^ , [ ] >`.
  ... Result in the type `polyTypeDefIR~tuple~ < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.

relation TypeArgument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument`

. If `typeArgument` has type `type`:
 .. Let `type` be `typeArgument`.
 .. Group type: `p`, `TC`, and `type`

  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `typeIR` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.

. Else if `typeArgument` has type `nonTypeName`:
 .. Let `nonTypeName` be `typeArgument`.
 .. Group nonTypeName: `p`, `TC`, and `nonTypeName`

  ... Let `tid` be `$name(nonTypeName)`.
  ... Result in `TID tid` and `[ ]`.
. Check that `typeArgument` has type `realTypeArgument`.
. Let `realTypeArgument` be `typeArgument`.
. If `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `VOID`:
 .. Group void: `p`, `TC`, and `VOID`

  ... Result in `VOID` and `[ ]`.

. Else if `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare: `p`, `TC`, and `_`

  ... Let `tid~impl~` be `$fresh_tid`.
  ... Result in `TID tid~impl~` and `[tid~impl~]`.

relation TypeArguments_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`

. If `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `p`, `TC`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `[ ]` and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `typeArgument~h~ :: typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument~h~ :: typeArgument~t~`

  ... <<TypeArgument_ok, `p TC |- typeArgument~h~ : typeArgumentIR~h~ # tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p TC |- typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^ : typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in `typeArgumentIR~h~ :: typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Sub_expl: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`

. Group : `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`

 .. Let `typeIR~a_canon~` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~a~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~b_canon~` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~b~`>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_expl_canon, `typeIR~a_canon~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b_canon~` after canonicalization>>.
 .. The relation holds.

relation Sub_expl_canon: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`

. Group equals: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`

 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
 .. The relation holds.
. Group not-equals: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`

 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are not the same type>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_expl_canon_neq, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~` when they are not the same type after canonicalization>>.
 .. The relation holds.

relation Sub_expl_canon_neq: `typeIR''''''` and `typeIR'''''''`

. If `typeIR''''''` has type `primitiveTypeIR`:
 .. Let `primitiveTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
 .. Check that `primitiveTypeIR` matches pattern `BOOL`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BIT < 1 >`.
 .. Group boolean-fixbit: `BOOL` and `BIT < 1 >`

  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR''''''` has type `numberTypeIR`:
 .. Let `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
 .. If `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
  ... Group arbint: `INT` and `typeIR`

   .... If `BOOL` is equal to `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... If `typeIR'''''''` has type `numberTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `numberTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... If let `INT < _ >` be `numberTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.

    ..... Else if let `BIT < _ >` be `numberTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `INT < nat >` be `numberTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `typeIR'''''''` has type `numberTypeIR`.
  ... Let `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`.
  ... Group fixint: `INT < nat >` and `numberTypeIR`

   .... If `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
    ..... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `INT < % >`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Check that `BIT < nat >` is equal to `numberTypeIR`.
   .... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `BIT < nat >` be `numberTypeIR`:
  ... Group fixbit: `BIT < nat >` and `typeIR`

   .... If 1 is equal to `nat`:
    ..... Check that `BOOL` is equal to `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... If `INT` is equal to `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... If `INT < nat >` is equal to `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... If `typeIR'''''''` has type `numberTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `numberTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that `numberTypeIR` matches pattern `BIT < % >`.
    ..... The relation holds.
. Group newtype: `typeIR` and `typeIR'`

 .. If `typeIR''''''` has type `newTypeIR`:
  ... Let `TYPE _ typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''''`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. If `typeIR'''''''` has type `newTypeIR`:
  ... Let `TYPE _ typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''''`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Group serenum: `typeIR` and `typeIR'`

 .. If `typeIR''''''` has type `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
  ... Check that `enumTypeIR` matches pattern `ENUM % # % { % }`.
  ... Let `ENUM _ # typeIR~a~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. If `typeIR'''''''` has type `enumTypeIR`:
  ... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`.
  ... Check that `enumTypeIR` matches pattern `ENUM % # % { % }`.
  ... Let `ENUM _ # typeIR~b~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. If `typeIR''''''` has type `defaultTypeIR`:
 .. Let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
 .. Group default: `DEFAULT` and `typeIR~b~`

  ... Check that `$is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR''''''')`.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR''''''` has type `invalidHeaderTypeIR`:
 .. Let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
 .. Group invalidheader: `HEADER_INVALID` and `typeIR`

  ... If `typeIR'''''''` has type `headerTypeIR`:
   .... Let `HEADER _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`.
   .... The relation holds.

  ... Else if `typeIR'''''''` has type `headerUnionTypeIR`:
   .... Let `HEADER_UNION _ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`.
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if `typeIR''''''` has type `sequenceTypeIR`:
 .. Let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`.
 .. If let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Group seq: `SEQ < typeIR~a~ >` and `typeIR`

   .... If `typeIR'''''''` has type `listTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `LIST < typeIR~b~ >` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for each `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` has type `tupleTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for each `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` has type `headerStackTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `typeIR~b~ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that the length of `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` is less than or equal to `n~size~`.
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for each `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` has type `structTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~b~ _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for each `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` has type `headerTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `HEADER _ { typeIR~b~ _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`.
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for each `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.

 .. Else if let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Group seqdefault: `SEQ < typeIR~a~ , ... >` and `typeIR`

   .... If `typeIR'''''''` has type `tupleTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''''`.
