relation Expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expression'''`

. If `expression'''` has type `booleanLiteral`:
 .. Let `booleanLiteral` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group literalExpression-boolean: `p`, `TC`, and `booleanLiteral`

  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `TRUE # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `FALSE # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `numberLiteral`:
 .. Let `numberLiteral` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group literalExpression-number: `p`, `TC`, and `numberLiteral`

  ... If let `D i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( INT LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `D i # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if let `n S i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( INT < n > LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `n S i # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if let `n W i` be `numberLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < n > LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `n W i # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `stringLiteral`:
 .. Let `" text "` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group literalExpression-stringLiteral: `p`, `TC`, and `" text "`

  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( STRING LCTK )`.
  ... Result in `" text " # expressionNoteIR`.
. Group referenceExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `expression`

 .. If `expression'''` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`:
  ... Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `expression'''`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?_ typeIR ctk _^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
  ... Result in `prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. If `THIS` is equal to `expression'''`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `` "this"`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?_ typeIR ctk _^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
  ... Result in `prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR`.
. If `expression'''` has type `defaultExpression`:
 .. Let `defaultExpression` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group defaultExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `...`

  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( DEFAULT LCTK )`.
  ... Result in `... # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `unaryExpression`:
 .. Let `unop expression` be `expression'''`.
 .. If `unop` matches pattern `!`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-lnot: `p`, `TC`, and `! expression`

   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_lnot)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `! typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.

 .. Else if `unop` matches pattern `~`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-bnot: `p`, `TC`, and `~ expression`

   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_bnot)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `~ typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group unaryExpression-uplusminus: `p`, `TC`, and `unop expression`

  ... If `unop` matches pattern `+`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if `unop` matches pattern `-`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `binaryExpression`:
 .. Let `expression~l~ binop expression~r~` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-plusminusmult: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[+, -, *]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_plusminusmult)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-satplusminus: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[|+|, |-|]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_satplusminus)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-divmod: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[/, %]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_divmod)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... If `ctk~r_reduced~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value~r~)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~r~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~r~` is greater than 0.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-shift: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<<, >>]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_shift)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... If `$is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
  ... If `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... If `$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... If `$is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~l_reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-equality: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[==, !=]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_cast~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_cast~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `$is_equalable_typeIR(typeIR~cast~)`.
  ... Let `ctk~cast~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_cast~, ctk~r_cast~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL ctk~cast~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_cast~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-comparison: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<=, >=, <, >]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_compare)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BOOL ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-bitwise: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&, ^, |]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_bitwise)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Check that `binop` matches pattern `++`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-concat: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ ++ expression~r~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_concat)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^` be `$result_concat(typeIR~l_reduced~, typeIR~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typeIR~reduced~` be `typeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ ++ typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-logical: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~l~ binop expression~r~`

  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_logical)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `ternaryExpression`:
 .. Let `expression~cond~ ? expression~true~ : expression~false~` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group ternaryExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~cond~ ? expression~true~ : expression~false~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR ctk~cond~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~cond~`.
  ... Check that `typeIR` has type `primitiveTypeIR`.
  ... Let `primitiveTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
  ... Check that `primitiveTypeIR` matches pattern `BOOL`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~true~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~true~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~false~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~false~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~true~, typedExpressionIR~false~)`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(typedExpressionIR~true_cast~, typedExpressionIR~false_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~true_cast~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~false_cast~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~false_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR~cast~) => ctk~cond~ =/= DYN`.
  ... Let `ctk` be `$joins_ctk([ctk~cond~, ctk~true_cast~, ctk~false_cast~])`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~cast~ ctk )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true_cast~ : typedExpressionIR~false_cast~ # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `castExpression`:
 .. Let `( type~t~ ) expression` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group castExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `( type~t~ ) expression`

  ... Let `typeIR~t~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type~t~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(p, TC) |- typeIR~t~`>> holds.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `ctk` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~t~`>>.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~t~ ctk )`.
  ... Result in `( typeIR~t~ ) typedExpressionIR # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `dataExpression`:
 .. Let `dataExpression` be `expression'''`.
 .. If `dataExpression` matches pattern `{#}`:
  ... Group dataExpression-invalid: `p`, `TC`, and `{#}`

   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( HEADER_INVALID LCTK )`.
   .... Result in `{#} # expressionNoteIR`.

 .. Else if let `{ dataElementExpression _ }` be `dataExpression`:
  ... If `dataElementExpression` has type `expressionList`:
   .... Let `expressionList` be `dataElementExpression`.
   .... Group dataExpression-sequence: `p`, `TC`, and `{ expressionList _ }`

    ..... Let `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_expressionList(expressionList)`.
    ..... If `...` is in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Check that `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `$flatten_expressionList(expressionList)`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>
--
+
for each `expression~e~` in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `ctk~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^ >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `$joins_ctk(ctk~e~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^ } # expressionNoteIR`.

    ..... Else if `...` is not in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Let `expression''^{asterisk}^` be `$rev_<expression>(expression~e~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Check that `expression''^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `_ :: _`.
     ...... Let `expression' :: expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^` be `expression''^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Check that `expression'` has type `defaultExpression`.
     ...... Let `defaultExpression` be `expression'`.
     ...... Let `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be `$rev_<expression>(expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Check that `...` is not in `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e_h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>
--
+
for each `expression~e_h~` in `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e_h~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e_h~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `$joins_ctk(ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.

  ... Else if `dataElementExpression` has type `recordElementExpression`:
   .... Let `recordElementExpression` be `dataElementExpression`.
   .... Group dataExpression-record: `p`, `TC`, and `{ recordElementExpression _ }`

    ..... If let `name~f~ = expression~f~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be `$name(name~f~)`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk~f~ )`.
     ...... Result in `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] } # expressionNoteIR`.

    ..... Else if let `name~f~ = expression~f~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be `$name(name~f~)`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] , ... }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk~f~ )`.
     ...... Result in `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.

    ..... Else if let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_namedExpressionList(namedExpressionList~t~)`.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ :: name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be `$name(name~f~)`
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ :: expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `$joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in `RECORD { nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^ } # expressionNoteIR`.

    ..... Else if let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_namedExpressionList(namedExpressionList~t~)`.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ :: name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be `$name(name~f~)`
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ :: expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `$joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR ctk )`.
     ...... Result in `RECORD { nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^ , ... } # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `errorAccessExpression`:
 .. Let `ERROR . member` be `expression'''`.
 .. Group errorAccessExpression: `p`, `TC`, and `ERROR . member`

  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`.
  ... Check that `ERROR . nameIR` is equal to `$find_value(p, TC, ` nameIR~error~)`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( ERROR LCTK )`.
  ... Result in `ERROR . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.

. Else if `expression'''` has type `memberAccessExpression`:
 .. Let `memberAccessBase . member` be `expression'''`.
 .. If `memberAccessBase` has type `prefixedTypeName`:
  ... Let `prefixedTypeName~base~` be `memberAccessBase`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-type: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedTypeName~base~ . member`

   .... Let `prefixedNameIR~base~` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName~base~)`.
   .... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_type(p, TC, prefixedNameIR~base~)`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `typeIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be `typeDefIR`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `enumTypeIR`.
   .... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM _ { nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~base~ LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.

   .... Else if let `ENUM _ # _ { nameIR~f~ = _ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( typeIR~base~ LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR # expressionNoteIR`.

 .. Else if `memberAccessBase` has type `expression`:
  ... Let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`.
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-expression: `p`, `TC`, and `expression~base~ . member`

   .... If `"size"` is equal to `$name(member)`:
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be `( BIT < 32 > LCTK )`.
    ..... Result in `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "size" # expressionNoteIR`.
   .... If `"lastIndex"` is equal to `$name(member)`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
     ...... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
