relation Argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `argument`

. Check that `argument` has type `expression`.
. Let `expression` be `argument`.
. Group expression: `p`, `TC`, and `expression`

 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR`.
. If let `name = expression` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-expression: `p`, `TC`, and `name = expression`

  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`.

. Else if let `name = _` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-dontcare: `p`, `TC`, and `name = _`

  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Result in `nameIR = _`.

. Else if `argument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare: `p`, `TC`, and `_`

  ... Result in `_`.

relation Lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`

. Check that `lvalue` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`.
. Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `lvalue`.
. Group referenceExpression-prefixedNonTypeName: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedNonTypeName`

 .. Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)`.
 .. Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
 .. Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
 .. Let `?direction typeIR ctk value^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
 .. Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
 .. Check that `value^?^` matches pattern `()`.
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Result in `prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )`.

 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Result in `prefixedNameIR # ( typeIR )`.
. If let `lvalue~base~ . member` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group memberAccess: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue~base~ . member`

  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`:
   .... Let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
   .... If `nameIR` = `"next"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

   .... Else if `nameIR` = `"last"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
     ...... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

  ... Else if `typeIR'` has type `structTypeIR`:
   .... Let `STRUCT _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

  ... Else if `typeIR'` has type `headerTypeIR`:
   .... Let `HEADER _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

  ... Else if `typeIR'` has type `headerUnionTypeIR`:
   .... Let `HEADER_UNION _ { typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(member)`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `$assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, (nameIR~f~, typeIR~f~)^{asterisk}^)`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~index~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group indexAccess: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue~base~ [ expression~index~ ]`

  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
  ... Let `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~index~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~index~ ctk~index~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~index~`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~index~, $compat_array_index)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... If `ctk~index~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `$to_number(value~index~)`.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~index~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~index~` is less than `n~size~`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

  ... Else if `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
   .... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~hi~ : expression~lo~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group sliceAccess: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue~base~ [ expression~hi~ : expression~lo~ ]`

  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Check that `$compat_bitslice_base(typeIR~base~)`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~hi~, $compat_bitslice_index)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~lo~, $compat_bitslice_index)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~hi_reduced~ ctk~hi_reduced~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~lo_reduced~ ctk~lo_reduced~ )` be `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`.
  ... Check that `ctk~hi_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int` be `$to_number(value~hi~)`.
  ... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~hi~` be `int`.
  ... Check that `ctk~lo_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int'` be `$to_number(value~lo~)`.
  ... Check that `int'` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~lo~` be `int'`.
  ... Check that `$is_valid_bitslice(typeIR~base~, n~lo~, n~hi~)`.
  ... Let `int''` be `n~hi~ - n~lo~ + 1`.
  ... Check that `int''` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~slice~` be `int''`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `BIT < n~slice~ >`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~ : typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~ ] # ( typeIR )`.
  ... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

. Else if let `( lvalue~base~ )` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group parenthesized: `p`, `TC`, and `( lvalue~base~ )`

  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ )` be `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be `( typedLvalueIR~base~ ) # ( typeIR~base~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedLvalueIR`.

relation Stmt_ok: `p'`, `TC'`, `f'`, and `statement`

. If `statement` has type `emptyStatement`:
 .. Let `emptyStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group emptyStatement: `p`, `TC`, `f`, and `;`

  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f'`,
        *  and the typed statement `;`.

. Else if `statement` has type `assignmentStatement`:
 .. Let `lvalue assignop expression ;` be `statement`.
 .. Check that `assignop` matches pattern `=`.
 .. Group assignmentStatement-eq: `p`, `TC`, `f`, and `lvalue = expression ;`

  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~l~` be `$typeof_lvalue(typedLvalueIR)`.
  ... Let `typeIR~r~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR, typeIR~l~)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f'`,
        *  and the typed statement `typedLvalueIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.

. Else if `statement` has type `callStatement`:
 .. Let `callStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group callStatement: `p`, `TC`, `f`, and `callStatement`

  ... If let `lvalue~routine~ ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~routine~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
   .... <<RoutineType_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `f'`,
          *  and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.

  ... Else if let `lvalue~routine~ < typeArgumentList > ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `routineTargetIR` be the result of <<RoutineTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~routine~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)`.
   .... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p' TC' |- typeArgument^{asterisk}^ : typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
   .... <<RoutineType_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : routineTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- routineTypeIR < [ ] # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `f'`,
          *  and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.

. Else if `statement` has type `directApplicationStatement`:
 .. Let `namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;` be `statement`.
 .. Group directApplicationStatement: `p`, `TC~0~`, `f`, and `namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;`

  ... Let `expressionIR # ( typeIR~object~ _ )` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `namedType ( )`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Check that `expressionIR` has type `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`.
  ... Check that `callExpressionIR` matches pattern `% ( % )`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Check that `$compat_direct_application(typeIR~object~)`.
  ... Let `nameIR~object~` be `"__direct_application"`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(p', TC', nameIR~object~, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())`.
  ... Let `lvalue` be `nameIR~object~ . "apply"`.
  ... Let `_`, `_`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `lvalue ( argumentList ) ;`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC~1~`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `callStatementIR`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `callStatementIR`.
  ... Check that `routineTargetIR` is equal to `` nameIR~object~ # ( typeIR~object~ CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `directApplicationStatementIR` be `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f'`,
        *  and the typed statement `directApplicationStatementIR`.

. Else if `statement` has type `exitStatement`:
 .. Let `exitStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group exitStatement: `p`, `TC`, `f`, and `EXIT ;`

  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f'`,
        *  and the typed statement `EXIT ;`.

. Else if `statement` has type `conditionalStatement`:
 .. Let `conditionalStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group conditionalStatement: `p`, `TC`, `f`, and `conditionalStatement`

  ... If let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `f'`,
          *  and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~`.

  ... Else if let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~ ELSE statement~else~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `TC~else~`, `f~else~`, and `statementIR~else~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~else~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `f~post~` be <<join_flow, the merged control flow of `f~then~` and `f~else~`>>.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
          *  and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `LOCAL`.
. If `statement` has type `returnStatement`:
 .. Let `returnStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group returnStatement: `LOCAL`, `TC`, `f`, and `returnStatement`

  ... If `returnStatement` matches pattern `RETURN ;`:
   .... Check that ?`VOID` is equal to `$find_return_type(TC')`.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `RET`,
          *  and the typed statement `RETURN ;`.

  ... Else if let `RETURN expression ;` be `returnStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR'^?^` be `$find_return_type(TC')`.
   .... Check that `typeIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typeIR~ret~` be `typeIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR, typeIR~ret~)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Result in 
          * the typing context `TC'`,
          * the abstract control flow `RET`,
          *  and the typed statement `RETURN typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.

. Else if `statement` has type `blockStatement`:
 .. Let `blockStatement` be `statement`.
 .. Group blockStatement: `LOCAL`, `TC~0~`, `f~0~`, and `blockStatement`

  ... <<Block_ok, `TC' f' |- blockStatement : TC~1~ f~1~ blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC~1~`,
        * the abstract control flow `f~1~`,
        *  and the typed statement `blockStatementIR`.

. Else if `statement` has type `switchStatement`:
 .. Let `SWITCH ( expression~switch~ ) { switchCaseList }` be `statement`.
 .. Group switchStatement-table: `LOCAL`, `TC`, `f`, and `SWITCH ( expression~switch~ ) { switchCaseList }`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR` has type `tableMetadataTypeIR`.
  ... Let `tableMetadataTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
  ... Check that `tableMetadataTypeIR` matches pattern `TABLE_ENUM % { % }`.
  ... Let `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `tableMetadataTypeIR`.
  ... Let `tid~table~` be `$strip_prefix($strip_suffix(tid~table_enum~, ")"), "action_list(")`.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_switchCaseList(switchCaseList)`.
  ... <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC' f' tid~table~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that `$distinct_<switchLabel>(switchLabel^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
        *  and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.
 .. Group switchStatement-general: `LOCAL`, `TC`, `f`, and `SWITCH ( expression~switch~ ) { switchCaseList }`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Check that `$compat_switch(typeIR~switch~)`.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_switchCaseList(switchCaseList)`.
  ... <<SwitchCases_general_ok, `TC' f' typeIR~switch~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that `$distinct_<switchLabel>(switchLabel^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
        * the typing context `TC'`,
        * the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
        *  and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.

relation BlockElementStmt_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `blockElementStatement`

. If `blockElementStatement` has type `constantDeclaration`:
 .. Let `constantDeclaration` be `blockElementStatement`.
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `constantDeclaration`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~`, `f`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `blockElementStatement` has type `variableDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `blockElementStatement`.
 .. Group variableDeclaration: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;`

  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0~) |- typeIR`>> holds.
   .... Check that `$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())`.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;`.
   .... Result in `TC~1~`, `f`, and `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... If `initializerOpt` has type `initializer`:
   .... Let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`.
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0~) |- typeIR`>> holds.
   .... Check that `$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~init~, typeIR)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())`.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?= typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
   .... Result in `TC~1~`, `f`, and `variableDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `blockElementStatement` has type `statement`:
 .. Let `statement` be `blockElementStatement`.
 .. Group statement: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `statement`

  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~post~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0~`, and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Result in `TC~1~`, `f~post~`, and `statementIR`.

relation BlockElementStmts_ok: `TC'`, `f'`, and `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`

. If `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC`, `f`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `TC'`, `f'`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `blockElementStatement~h~ :: blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^` be `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC~0~`, `f~0~`, and `blockElementStatement~h~ :: blockElementStatement~t~`

  ... <<BlockElementStmt_ok, `TC' f' |- blockElementStatement~h~ : TC~1~ f~1~ blockElementStatementIR~h~`>>.
  ... <<BlockElementStmts_ok, `TC~1~ f~1~ |- blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ f~2~ blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TC~2~`, `f~2~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Block_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementList }`

. Group : `TC~0~`, `f`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementList }`

 .. Let `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_blockElementStatementList(blockElementStatementList)`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `$enter(TC~0~)`.
 .. <<BlockElementStmts_ok, `TC~1~ f |- blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ f~post~ blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Let `TC~3~` be `$exit(TC~2~)`.
 .. Let `blockStatementIR` be `annotationList { blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Result in `TC~3~`, `f~post~`, and `blockStatementIR`.

relation Parameter_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `annotationList direction type name initializerOpt`

. If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty: `p`, `TC`, and `annotationList direction type name`

  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound` be `$union_set<tid>($bound(p, TC), { tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ })`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Result in `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR ?()` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. If `initializerOpt` has type `initializer`:
 .. Let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`.
 .. Group initializer: `p`, `TC`, and `annotationList direction type name = expression~init~`

  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound` be `$union_set<tid>($bound(p, TC), { tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ })`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `bound |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~init~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~init~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR~init~>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~init~, typeIR)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Let `value~init~` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR ?= value~init~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Parameters_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `parameter^{asterisk}^`

. If `parameter^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
