     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = D n :`.

    ..... Else if `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.LARGEST_WINS`:
     ...... Let `n~last~` be `$find_table_priority_last(tableContext')`.
     ...... Let `n~delta~` be `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.DELTA`.
     ...... Let `n` be `n~last~ + n~delta~`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `$add_table_priority(tableContext', n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = D n :`.

. Else if let `?tableEntryPriority` be `tableEntryPriority''^?^`:
 .. If let `PRIORITY = numberLiteral :` be `tableEntryPriority`:
  ... Group specified-number: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, `TBLS`, and ?`PRIORITY = numberLiteral :`

   .... If `tableContext'.MODE` matches pattern `PRI`:
    ..... Check that `tableContext'.ENTRIES.CONST`.
    ..... If `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` = `[ ]`:
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(numberLiteral)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `tableContext'`[PRIORITIES.INIT = true].
     ...... Let `TBLC~2~` be `$add_table_priority(TBLC~1~, n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `?PRIORITY = numberLiteral :`.

    ..... Else if `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` =/= `[ ]`:
     ...... Check that `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.INIT`.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(numberLiteral)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `$add_table_priority(tableContext', n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = numberLiteral :`.

   .... Else if `tableContext'.MODE` matches pattern `PRILPM`:
    ..... Check that `tableContext'.ENTRIES.CONST`.
    ..... If `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` = `[ ]`:
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(numberLiteral)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `tableContext'`[PRIORITIES.INIT = true].
     ...... Let `TBLC~2~` be `$add_table_priority(TBLC~1~, n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `?PRIORITY = numberLiteral :`.

    ..... Else if `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` =/= `[ ]`:
     ...... Check that `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.INIT`.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(numberLiteral)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `$add_table_priority(tableContext', n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = numberLiteral :`.

 .. Else if let `PRIORITY = ( expression ) :` be `tableEntryPriority`:
  ... Group specified-expression: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, `TBLS`, and ?`PRIORITY = ( expression ) :`

   .... If `tableContext'.MODE` matches pattern `PRI`:
    ..... Check that `tableContext'.ENTRIES.CONST`.
    ..... If `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` = `[ ]`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
     ...... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `tableContext'`[PRIORITIES.INIT = true].
     ...... Let `TBLC~2~` be `$add_table_priority(TBLC~1~, n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `?PRIORITY = ( typedExpressionIR ) :`.

    ..... Else if `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` =/= `[ ]`:
     ...... Check that `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.INIT`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
     ...... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `$add_table_priority(tableContext', n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = ( typedExpressionIR ) :`.

   .... Else if `tableContext'.MODE` matches pattern `PRILPM`:
    ..... Check that `tableContext'.ENTRIES.CONST`.
    ..... If `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` = `[ ]`:
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
     ...... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `tableContext'`[PRIORITIES.INIT = true].
     ...... Let `TBLC~2~` be `$add_table_priority(TBLC~1~, n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `?PRIORITY = ( typedExpressionIR ) :`.

    ..... Else if `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.VALUES` =/= `[ ]`:
     ...... Check that `tableContext'.PRIORITIES.INIT`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
     ...... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
     ...... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
     ...... Let `n` be `int`.
     ...... Let `TBLC~1~` be `$add_table_priority(tableContext', n)`.
     ...... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `?PRIORITY = ( typedExpressionIR ) :`.

relation TableEntry_ok: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `tableEntry`

. If let `constOpt tableEntryPriority keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;` be `tableEntry`:
 .. Group priority: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `constOpt tableEntryPriority keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;`

  ... <<TableEntry_keyset_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ |- keysetExpression : TBLS keysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... <<TableEntry_action_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ |- tableActionReference : tableActionReferenceIR`>>.
  ... <<TableEntry_priority_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ TBLS |- ?tableEntryPriority : TBLC~1~ tableEntryPriorityOptIR`>>.
  ... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
  ... Let `tableEntryIR` be `constOptIR tableEntryPriorityOptIR keysetExpressionIR : tableActionReferenceIR annotationList ;`.
  ... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tableEntryIR`.

. Else if let `constOpt keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;` be `tableEntry`:
 .. Group non-priority: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `constOpt keysetExpression : tableActionReference annotationList ;`

  ... <<TableEntry_keyset_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ |- keysetExpression : TBLS keysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... <<TableEntry_action_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ |- tableActionReference : tableActionReferenceIR`>>.
  ... <<TableEntry_priority_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ TBLS |- ?() : TBLC~1~ tableEntryPriorityOptIR`>>.
  ... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
  ... Let `tableEntryIR` be `constOptIR tableEntryPriorityOptIR keysetExpressionIR : tableActionReferenceIR annotationList ;`.
  ... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tableEntryIR`.

relation TableEntries_ok: `TC`, `TBLC'`, and `tableEntry^{asterisk}^`

. If `tableEntry^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC`, `TBLC`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `TBLC'` and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `tableEntry~h~ :: tableEntry~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableEntry^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `tableEntry~h~ :: tableEntry~t~`

  ... <<TableEntry_ok, `TC TBLC' |- tableEntry~h~ : TBLC~1~ tableEntryIR~h~`>>.
  ... <<TableEntries_ok, `TC TBLC~1~ |- tableEntry~t~^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~2~ tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `tableEntryIR~h~ :: tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation TableProperty_ok: `TC`, `TBLC~0'~`, and `tableProperty`

. If let `KEY = { tableKeyList }` be `tableProperty`:
 .. Group key: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `KEY = { tableKeyList }`

  ... Let `tableKey^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_tableKeyList(tableKeyList)`.
  ... <<TableKeys_ok, `TC TBLC~0'~ |- tableKey^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~1~ tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `KEY = { tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^ }`.

. Else if let `ACTIONS = { tableActionList }` be `tableProperty`:
 .. Group actions: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `ACTIONS = { tableActionList }`

  ... Let `tableAction^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_tableActionList(tableActionList)`.
  ... <<TableActions_ok, `TC TBLC~0'~ |- tableAction^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~1~ tableActionIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `ACTIONS = { tableActionIR^{asterisk}^ }`.

. Else if let `annotationList constOpt ENTRIES = { tableEntryList }` be `tableProperty`:
 .. Group entries: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `annotationList constOpt ENTRIES = { tableEntryList }`

  ... Let `tableEntry^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_tableEntryList(tableEntryList)`.
  ... Check that `the length of TBLC~0'~.KEYS = 0 => the length of tableEntry^{asterisk}^ = 0`.
  ... Let `TBLC~1~` be `TBLC~0'~`[ENTRIES.SIZE = the length of `tableEntry^{asterisk}^`].
  ... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
  ... Let `TBLC~2~` be `TBLC~1~`[ENTRIES.CONST = `constOptIR` is equal to ?`CONST`].
  ... <<TableEntries_ok, `TC TBLC~2~ |- tableEntry^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~3~ tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLC~3~` and `annotationList constOptIR ENTRIES = { tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^ }`.

. Else if let `annotationList constOpt tableCustomName initializer ;` be `tableProperty`:
 .. Group default-action: `TC`, `TBLC`, and `annotationList constOpt tableCustomName initializer ;`

  ... Check that `"default_action"` is equal to `$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)`.
  ... <<TableDefaultAction_ok, `TC TBLC~0'~ |- initializer : tableActionReferenceIR`>>.
  ... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
  ... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR DEFAULT_ACTION = tableActionReferenceIR ;`.
  ... Result in `TBLC~0'~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
 .. Let `annotationList constOpt tableCustomName = expression ;` be `tableProperty`.
 .. Group custom: `TC`, `tableContext`, and `annotationList constOpt tableCustomName = expression ;`

  ... If `"size"` is equal to `$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... If `$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~0'~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
   .... If `$is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~0'~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
   .... If `$is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM "size" = typedExpressionIR ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~0'~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
  ... If `"largest_priority_wins"` is equal to `$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR`>>.
   .... Let `value'` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `value'` has type `primitiveValue`.
   .... Let `primitiveValue` be `value'`.
   .... Check that `primitiveValue` matches pattern `B %`.
   .... Let `B b~largest_priority_wins~` be `primitiveValue`.
   .... Let `TBLC~1~` be `TBLC~0'~`[PRIORITIES.LARGEST_WINS = `b~largest_priority_wins~`].
   .... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
   .... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "largest_priority_wins" = B b~largest_priority_wins~ ;`.
   .... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
  ... If `"priority_delta"` is equal to `$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... If `$is_arbitrary_int_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
    ..... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
    ..... Let `n~delta~` be `int`.
    ..... Check that `n~delta~` is greater than 0.
    ..... Let `TBLC~1~` be `TBLC~0'~`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `n~delta~`].
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n~delta~ ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
   .... If `$is_fixed_int_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
    ..... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
    ..... Let `n~delta~` be `int`.
    ..... Check that `n~delta~` is greater than 0.
    ..... Let `TBLC~1~` be `TBLC~0'~`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `n~delta~`].
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n~delta~ ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
   .... If `$is_fixed_bit_typeIR(typeIR)`:
    ..... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `int` be `$to_number(value)`.
    ..... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
    ..... Let `n~delta~` be `int`.
    ..... Check that `n~delta~` is greater than 0.
    ..... Let `TBLC~1~` be `TBLC~0'~`[PRIORITIES.DELTA = `n~delta~`].
    ..... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
    ..... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM_CONST "priority_delta" = D n~delta~ ;`.
    ..... Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tablePropertyIR`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)`.
  ... If `nameIR =/= "size" /\ nameIR =/= "largest_priority_wins" /\ nameIR =/= "priority_delta"`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `constOptIR` be `$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)`.
   .... Let `tablePropertyIR` be `annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM nameIR = typedExpressionIR ;`.
   .... Result in `TBLC~0'~` and `tablePropertyIR`.

relation TableProperties_ok: `TC`, `TBLC'`, and `tableProperty^{asterisk}^`

. If `tableProperty^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC`, `TBLC`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `TBLC'` and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `tableProperty~h~ :: tableProperty~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableProperty^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `tableProperty~h~ :: tableProperty~t~`

  ... <<TableProperty_ok, `TC TBLC' |- tableProperty~h~ : TBLC~1~ tablePropertyIR~h~`>>.
  ... <<TableProperties_ok, `TC TBLC~1~ |- tableProperty~t~^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~2~ tablePropertyIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLC~2~` and `tablePropertyIR~h~ :: tablePropertyIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Table_ok: `TC` and `tableProperty^{asterisk}^`

. Group : `TC` and `tableProperty`

 .. Check that `$count_table_keys(tableProperty^{asterisk}^)` is less than or equal to 1.
 .. Check that `$count_table_actions(tableProperty^{asterisk}^)` is equal to 1.
 .. Let `TBLC~0~` be `$empty_tableContext`.
 .. <<TableProperties_ok, `TC TBLC~0~ |- tableProperty^{asterisk}^ : TBLC~1~ tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Result in `TBLC~1~` and `tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`.

relation TableType_ok: `TC~0~`, `TBLC`, and `name`

. Group : `TC~0~`, `TBLC`, and `name`

 .. Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
 .. Let `tid~enum~` be `"action_list(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"`.
 .. Let `(prefixedNameIR~action~, _^{asterisk}^, _)^{asterisk}^` be `TBLC.ACTIONS`.
 .. Let `id~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `id~enum_field~` be `$flatten_prefixedNameIR(prefixedNameIR~action~)`
--
+
for each `prefixedNameIR~action~` in `prefixedNameIR~action~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~table_enum~` be `TABLE_ENUM tid~enum~ { id~enum_field~^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Let `value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `value~enum_field~` be `TABLE_ENUM tid~enum~ . id~enum_field~`
--
+
for each `id~enum_field~` in `id~enum_field~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `varTypeIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `varTypeIR~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `varTypeIR~enum_field~` be `typeIR~table_enum~ LCTK ?value~enum_field~`
--
+
for each `value~enum_field~` in `value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `$add_vars(BLOCK, TC~0~, tid~enum~ ++ "." ++ id~enum_field~^{asterisk}^, varTypeIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `tid~struct~` be `"apply_result(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"`.
 .. Let `typeIR~table_struct~` be `TABLE_STRUCT tid~struct~ { [BOOL "hit" ;, BOOL "miss" ;, typeIR~table_enum~ "action_run" ;] }`.
 .. Let `typeIR~table~` be `TABLE nameIR # typeIR~table_struct~`.
 .. Result in `TC~1~` and `typeIR~table~`.

relation ControlLocalDecl_ok: `TC~0~` and `controlLocalDeclaration`

. If `controlLocalDeclaration` has type `constantDeclaration`:
 .. Let `constantDeclaration` be `controlLocalDeclaration`.
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `TC~0~` and `constantDeclaration`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `constantDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `controlLocalDeclaration` has type `instantiation`:
 .. Let `instantiation` be `controlLocalDeclaration`.
 .. Group instantiation: `TC~0~` and `instantiation`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `instantiationIR`.

. Else if `controlLocalDeclaration` has type `variableDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `controlLocalDeclaration`.
 .. Group variableDeclaration: `TC~0~` and `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;`

  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~) |- typeIR`>> holds.
   .... Check that `$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())`.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;`.
   .... Result in `TC~1~` and `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... If `initializerOpt` has type `initializer`:
   .... Let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`.
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~) |- typeIR`>> holds.
   .... Check that `$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~init~, typeIR)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())`.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR ?= typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
   .... Result in `TC~1~` and `variableDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `controlLocalDeclaration` has type `actionDeclaration`:
 .. Let `actionDeclaration` be `controlLocalDeclaration`.
 .. Group actionDeclaration: `TC~0~` and `actionDeclaration`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `actionDeclaration`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `actionDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `actionDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `actionDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `controlLocalDeclaration` has type `tableDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }` be `controlLocalDeclaration`.
 .. Group tableDeclaration: `TC~0~` and `annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }`

  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[LOCAL.KIND = `TABLE_APPLY_METHOD`].
  ... Let `tableProperty^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_tablePropertyList(tablePropertyList)`.
  ... <<Table_ok, `TC~1~ |- tableProperty^{asterisk}^ : TBLC tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... <<TableType_ok, `TC~1~ TBLC |- name : TC~2~ typeIR~table~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `$add_var(BLOCK, TC~2~, nameIR, typeIR~table~ DYN ?())`.
  ... Let `tableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList TABLE typeIR~table~ nameIR { tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in `TC~3~` and `tableDeclarationIR`.

relation ControlLocalDecls_ok: `TC'` and `controlLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^`

. If `controlLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC` and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `TC'` and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `controlLocalDeclaration~h~ :: controlLocalDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `controlLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC~0~` and `controlLocalDeclaration~h~ :: controlLocalDeclaration~t~`

  ... <<ControlLocalDecl_ok, `TC' |- controlLocalDeclaration~h~ : TC~1~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~`>>.
  ... <<ControlLocalDecls_ok, `TC~1~ |- controlLocalDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TC~2~` and `controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~ :: controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Decl_ok: `p'`, `TC~0~`, and `declaration`

. If `declaration` has type `constantDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList CONST type name = expression~value~ ;` be `declaration`.
 .. Group constantDeclaration: `p`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList CONST type name = expression~value~ ;`

  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `$bound(p', TC~0~) |- typeIR`>> holds.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~value~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~value~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR~value~>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~value~, typeIR)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~value_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Eval_static, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~value_cast~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR LCTK ?value)`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `constantDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `instantiation`:
 .. Let `instantiation` be `declaration`.
 .. If let `annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;` be `instantiation`:
  ... Group instantiation-non-objectInitializer: `p`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;`

   .... If `type` has type `prefixedTypeName`:
    ..... Let `prefixedTypeName` be `type`.
    ..... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
    ..... <<ConstructorType_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... <<Inst_ok, `p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `instantiationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~object~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) nameIR ?() ;`.
    ..... Result in `TC~1~` and `instantiationIR`.

   .... Else if `type` has type `specializedType`:
    ..... Let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >` be `type`.
    ..... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)`.
    ..... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- typeArgument^{asterisk}^ : typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
    ..... <<ConstructorType_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<Inst_ok, `p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `instantiationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~object~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) nameIR ?() ;`.
    ..... Result in `TC~1~` and `instantiationIR`.

 .. Else if let `annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;` be `instantiation`:
  ... Group instantiation-objectInitializer: `p`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;`

   .... If `type` has type `prefixedTypeName`:
    ..... Let `prefixedTypeName` be `type`.
    ..... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
    ..... <<ConstructorType_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... <<Inst_ok, `p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~object~>>)`.
    ..... Check that `typeIR~object~` has type `specializedTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `typeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ > < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR~object~`.
    ..... Check that `typeIR` has type `externObjectTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~extern~` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is equal to `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, "this", typeIR~object~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)`.
    ..... <<Decls_object_ok, `p' TC~1~ { [ ] } { [ ] } |- objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^ : frame~init~ rdenv~init~ objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `tid^{asterisk}^` be `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `theta` be `{ tid : typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ }`.
    ..... Let `rdenv~init_subst~` be `$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv~extern~, rdenv~init~)`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~object_init~` be `EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~init_subst~ < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >`.
    ..... Check that `$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object_init~)`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
    ..... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object_init~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `instantiationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~object_init~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) nameIR ?= { objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^ } ;`.
    ..... Result in `TC~2~` and `instantiationIR`.

   .... Else if `type` has type `specializedType`:
    ..... Let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >` be `type`.
    ..... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)`.
    ..... <<TypeArguments_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- typeArgument^{asterisk}^ : typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)`.
    ..... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
          * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC~0~`>>
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)`.
    ..... <<ConstructorType_ok, `p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... <<Inst_ok, `p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
    ..... Check that `$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~object~>>)`.
    ..... Check that `typeIR~object~` has type `specializedTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `typeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ > < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR~object~`.
    ..... Check that `typeIR` has type `externObjectTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~extern~` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is equal to `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, "this", typeIR~object~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)`.
    ..... <<Decls_object_ok, `p' TC~1~ { [ ] } { [ ] } |- objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^ : frame~init~ rdenv~init~ objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `tid^{asterisk}^` be `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ ++ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `theta` be `{ tid : typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ }`.
    ..... Let `rdenv~init_subst~` be `$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv~extern~, rdenv~init~)`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~object_init~` be `EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~init_subst~ < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >`.
    ..... Check that `$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object_init~)`.
    ..... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
    ..... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object_init~ CTK ?())`.
    ..... Let `instantiationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~object_init~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) nameIR ?= { objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^ } ;`.
    ..... Result in `TC~2~` and `instantiationIR`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `functionDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `declaration`.
 .. Group functionDeclaration: `p`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement`

  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)`.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be `$name(typeParameter)`
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_types(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)`.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~1~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `TC~2~`[LOCAL.KIND = `FUNCTION -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... <<Block_ok, `TC~3~ CONT |- blockStatement : _ f blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... If `f` matches pattern `RET`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `functionTypeIR` be `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `functionTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p', TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_routine_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `TC~4~` and `functionDeclarationIR`.
  ... If `typeIR~ret~` is equal to `VOID`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `functionTypeIR` be `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `functionTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p', TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_routine_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `TC~4~` and `functionDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `actionDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `declaration`.
 .. Group actionDeclaration: `p`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement`

  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[LOCAL.KIND = `ACTION`].
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)`.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~1~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... <<Block_ok, `TC~2~ CONT |- blockStatement : _ _ blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR` be `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p', TC~0~) |- functionTypeIR`>> holds.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `$add_routine_non_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, functionTypeIR)`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Let `actionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `TC~3~` and `actionDeclarationIR`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. If `declaration` has type `errorDeclaration`:
 .. Let `ERROR { nameList }` be `declaration`.
 .. Group errorDeclaration: `GLOBAL`, `TC~0~`, and `ERROR { nameList }`

  ... Let `name^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_nameList(nameList)`.
  ... Let `nameIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`
--
+
for each `name` in `name^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `$distinct_<nameIR>(nameIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." ++ nameIR`
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `value~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~error~` be `ERROR . nameIR`
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^, ERROR LCTK ?value~error~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `ERROR { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `matchKindDeclaration`:
 .. Let `MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }` be `declaration`.
 .. Group matchKindDeclaration: `GLOBAL`, `TC~0~`, and `MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }`

  ... Let `name^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_nameList(nameList)`.
  ... Let `nameIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`
--
+
for each `name` in `name^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `$distinct_<nameIR>(nameIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~match_kind~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~match_kind~` be `MATCH_KIND . nameIR`
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR^{asterisk}^, MATCH_KIND LCTK ?value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Result in `TC~1~` and `MATCH_KIND { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `externFunctionDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;` be `declaration`.
 .. Group externFunctionDeclaration: `GLOBAL`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;`

  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)`.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be `$name(typeParameter)`
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `$add_types(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_FUNCTION -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)`.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~2~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR` be `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `functionTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
  ... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(GLOBAL, TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_routine_overload(GLOBAL, TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
  ... Let `externFunctionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList EXTERN typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in `TC~4~` and `externFunctionDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `externObjectDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList EXTERN nonTypeName typeParameterListOpt { methodPrototypeList }` be `declaration`.
 .. Group externObjectDeclaration: `GLOBAL`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList EXTERN nonTypeName typeParameterListOpt { methodPrototypeList }`

  ... Let `methodPrototype^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_methodPrototypeList(methodPrototypeList)`.
  ... Let `(methodPrototype~constructor~^{asterisk}^, methodPrototype~method~^{asterisk}^)` be `$split_constructors(methodPrototype^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[BLOCK.KIND = `EXTERN`].
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)`.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be `$name(typeParameter)`
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_types(BLOCK, TC~1~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$name(nonTypeName)`.
  ... <<ExternMethods_ok, `TC~2~ nameIR |- methodPrototype~method~^{asterisk}^ : TC~3~ methodPrototypeIR~method~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~extern~` be `EXTERN nameIR TC~3~.BLOCK.RDENV`.
  ... Let `typeDefIR~extern~` be `typeIR~extern~ < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , [ ] >`.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_type(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR, typeDefIR~extern~)`.
  ... Let `TC~5~` be `TC~4~`[BLOCK.KIND = `EXTERN`].
  ... Let `TC~6~` be `$add_types(BLOCK, TC~5~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... <<ExternConstructors_ok, `TC~6~ nameIR |- methodPrototype~constructor~^{asterisk}^ : TC~7~ methodPrototypeIR~constructor~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `TC~8~` be `TC~4~`[GLOBAL.CDENV = `TC~7~.GLOBAL.CDENV`].
  ... Let `externObjectDeclarationIR` be `annotationList EXTERN nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , [ ] > { methodPrototypeIR~constructor~^{asterisk}^ ++ methodPrototypeIR~method~^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in `TC~8~` and `externObjectDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declaration` has type `parserDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList PARSER name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { parserLocalDeclarationList parserStateList }` be `declaration`.
 .. Check that `typeParameterListOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`.
 .. Group parserDeclaration: `GLOBAL`, `TC~0~`, and `annotationList PARSER name ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { parserLocalDeclarationList parserStateList }`

  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[BLOCK.KIND = `PARSER`].
  ... Let `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_constructorParameterListOpt(constructorParameterListOpt)`.
  ... <<ConstructorParameters_ok, `BLOCK TC~1~ |- constructorParameter^{asterisk}^ : constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ # tid^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `constructorParameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `constructorParameterTypeIR` be `$constructorParameterIR(constructorParameterIR)`
--
+
for each `constructorParameterIR` in `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `$add_parameters(BLOCK, TC~1~, constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)`.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid'^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
