 .. Let `declaration^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_p4program(p4program)`.
 .. Let `TC~0~` be `$empty_typingContext`.
 .. <<Decls_ok, `GLOBAL TC~0~ |- declaration^{asterisk}^ : TC~1~ declarationIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Result in `TC~1~` and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;`.

relation Call_convention_expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ _ _^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

. If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
 .. Group in: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `IN typeIR~param~ _ _`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~arg~, typeIR~param~)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
. Group out-inout: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ _ _`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>> holds.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.

 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>> holds.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
. If `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `typeIR~param~ _ _`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`

  ... If `actctxt` matches pattern `ACTION`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~arg~, typeIR~param~)`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.

  ... Else if `actctxt` matches pattern `NOACTION`:
   .... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~arg~` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
   .... Check that `ctk~arg~` does not match pattern `DYN`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.

relation Call_convention_argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `argumentIR`

. Check that `argumentIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
. Let `typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`.
. Group typedExpression: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `typedExpressionIR`

 .. <<Call_convention_expr_ok, `p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR @ typedExpressionIR : typedExpressionIR~cast~`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `nameIR = typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpression: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`

  ... <<Call_convention_expr_ok, `p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR @ typedExpressionIR : typedExpressionIR~cast~`>>.
  ... Result in `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`.

. Else if let `nameIR = _` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-dontcare: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `nameIR = _`

  ... Let `direction _ _ _^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `nameIR = _`.

. Else if `argumentIR` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `_`

  ... Let `direction _ _ _^?^` be `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `_`.

relation Call_convention_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`

. If `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
