  ... Result in `[ ]`.

. Else if let `parameterTypeIR~h~ :: parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `_ :: _`.
 .. Let `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR~h~ :: parameterTypeIR~t~`, and `argumentIR~h~ :: argumentIR~t~`

  ... <<Call_convention_argument_ok, `p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR~h~ @ argumentIR~h~ : argumentIR~h_cast~`>>.
  ... <<Call_convention_ok, `p TC actctxt |- parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^ @ argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^ : argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^`>>.
