relation ConstructorType_ok: `p`, `TC`, `prefixedNameIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`

. Group : `p`, `TC`, `prefixedNameIR`, `typeArgumentIR`, and `argumentIR`

 .. Let `(rid, constructorTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` be `$find_constructor_overloaded(TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Check that `(rid, constructorTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
 .. Let `?(cid, constructorTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(rid, constructorTypeDefIR, id*)^?^`.
 .. Let `(constructorTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `$specialize_constructorTypeDef(constructorTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `bound` be `$union_set<tid>($bound(p, TC), { tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ })`.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `bound |- constructorTypeIR`>> holds.
 .. Result in `constructorTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Inst_ok: `cursor'`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`

. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. Group package: `GLOBAL`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR`, `tid~infer~`, `argumentIR`, and `id~default~`

 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR` has type `packageObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PACKAGE < _^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `$align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `inference` be `$infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR'^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR'^?^` be `$find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)`
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`, for each `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR'^?^`
--
+
for each `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `$subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)`
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~object_inferred~` be `$subst_type(inference, typeIR~object~)`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object_inferred~`.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `$bound(GLOBAL, TC) |- constructorTypeIR~inferred~`>> holds.
 .. Check that `$instantiable(GLOBAL, TC, instctxt, typeIR~object_inferred~)`.
 .. <<Call_convention_ok, `BLOCK TC NOACTION |- parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ @ argumentIR^{asterisk}^ : argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Result in `typeIR~object_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Group non-package: `p`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR`, `tid~infer~`, `argumentIR`, and `id~default~`

 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Check that `$is_package_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~object~>>)`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `$filter_default_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `$align_parameters(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `inference` be `$infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)`.
 .. Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR^?^` be `$find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)`
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `typeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`, for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `?typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ ++ typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `$subst_parameterType(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)`
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~object_inferred~` be `$subst_type(inference, typeIR~object~)`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~object_inferred~`.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `$bound(cursor', TC) |- constructorTypeIR~inferred~`>> holds.
 .. Check that `$instantiable(cursor', TC, instctxt, typeIR~object_inferred~)`.
 .. <<Call_convention_ok, `cursor' TC NOACTION |- parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ @ argumentIR^{asterisk}^ : argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Result in `typeIR~object_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.

relation SwitchLabel_table_ok: `TC`, `tid~table~`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`

. Group : `TC`, `tid~table~`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`

 .. If true is equal to `bool`:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. If `switchLabel` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`:
  ... Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `switchLabel`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)`.
  ... Check that `prefixedNameIR` matches pattern `` %`.
  ... Let `` nameIR~label~` be `prefixedNameIR`.
  ... Let `tid~table_enum~` be `"action_list(" ++ tid~table~ ++ ")"`.
  ... Let `id~label~` be `tid~table_enum~ ++ "." ++ nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(LOCAL, TC, ` id~label~)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?_ typeIR~label~ ctk~label~ value^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Check that `value^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?value~label~` be `value^?^`.
  ... Check that `value~label~` is equal to `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ . nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be `` nameIR~label~ # ( typeIR~label~ ctk~label~ )`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label~`.

relation SwitchCase_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`

. Group : `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`

 .. If let `switchLabel : blockStatement` be `switchCase`:
  ... <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... <<Block_ok, `TC f |- blockStatement : TC~post~ f~post~ blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `f~post~`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.

 .. Else if let `switchLabel :` be `switchCase`:
  ... <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR :`.
  ... Result in `f`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.

relation SwitchCases_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, and `switchCase^{asterisk}^`

. If `switchCase^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `f`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCase^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, and `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~`

  ... Let `b~last~` be `switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... <<SwitchCase_table_ok, `TC f tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchCase~h~ : f~h~ switchCaseIR~h~ # switchLabel~h~`>>.
  ... <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC f~h~ tid~table~ |- switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^ : f~t~ switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `f~t~`, `switchCaseIR~h~ :: switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `switchLabel~h~ :: switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation SwitchLabel_general_ok: `TC`, `typeIR`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`

. Group : `TC`, `typeIR`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`

 .. If true is equal to `bool`:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. If `switchLabel` has type `expressionNonBrace`:
  ... Let `expressionNonBrace~label~` be `switchLabel`.
  ... Let `expression~label~` be `$expressionNonBrace(expressionNonBrace~label~)`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~label~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~label~, typeIR)`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typedExpressionIR~label_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `_ # ( _ ctk )` be `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.

relation SwitchCase_general_ok: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`

. Group : `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`

 .. If let `switchLabel : blockStatement` be `switchCase`:
  ... <<SwitchLabel_general_ok, `TC typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... <<Block_ok, `TC f |- blockStatement : TC~post~ f~post~ blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `f~post~`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.

 .. Else if let `switchLabel :` be `switchCase`:
  ... <<SwitchLabel_general_ok, `TC typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR :`.
  ... Result in `f`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.

relation SwitchCases_general_ok: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, and `switchCase^{asterisk}^`

. If `switchCase^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `f`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCase^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `TC`, `f`, `typeIR~switch~`, and `switchCase~h~ :: switchCase~t~`

  ... Let `b~last~` be `switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... <<SwitchCase_general_ok, `TC f typeIR~switch~ b~last~ |- switchCase~h~ : f~h~ switchCaseIR~h~ # switchLabel~h~`>>.
  ... <<SwitchCases_general_ok, `TC f~h~ typeIR~switch~ |- switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^ : f~t~ switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `f~t~`, `switchCaseIR~h~ :: switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `switchLabel~h~ :: switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Decl_object_ok: `p`, `TC~0~`, `frame`, `rdenv`, and `objectDeclaration`

. If `objectDeclaration` has type `functionDeclaration`:
 .. Let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `objectDeclaration`.
 .. Group functionDeclaration: `p`, `TC~0~`, `frame`, `rdenv`, and `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement`

  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~`[BLOCK.KIND = `EXTERN`].
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~`[BLOCK.FRAME = `frame`].
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)`.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be `$name(typeParameter)`
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `$add_types(LOCAL, TC~2~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, TID tid~expl~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be `$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)`.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~3~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `TC~5~` be `TC~4~`[LOCAL.KIND = `EXTERN_METHOD -> typeIR~ret~`].
  ... <<Block_ok, `TC~5~ CONT |- blockStatement : _ f blockStatementIR`>>.
  ... If `f` matches pattern `RET`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p, TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `rdenv~init~` be `$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `frame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
  ... If `typeIR~ret~` is equal to `VOID`:
   .... Let `rid` be `$rid(name, parameterList)`.
   .... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ >`.
   .... Check that <<RoutineTypeDef_wf, `$bound(p, TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR`>> holds.
   .... Let `rdenv~init~` be `$update_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be `$name(name)`.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `frame`, `rdenv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `objectDeclaration` has type `instantiation`:
 .. Let `instantiation` be `objectDeclaration`.
 .. Group instantiation: `p`, `TC~0~`, `frame`, `rdenv`, and `instantiation`

  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~0~`,
        * and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Let `_ _ _ < _ > ( _ ) nameIR _ ;` be `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR'^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC~1~, ` nameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?varTypeIR` be `varTypeIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `frame~init~` be `$update_map<id, varTypeIR>(frame, nameIR, varTypeIR)`.
  ... Result in `frame~init~`, `rdenv`, and `instantiationIR`.

relation Decls_object_ok: `p`, `TC`, `frame'`, `rdenv'`, and `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`

. If `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
