relation Expr_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expressionIR # ( _ _ )`

. If `expressionIR` has type `prefixedNameIR`:
 .. Let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `prefixedNameIR # ( _ _ )`

  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?direction _ ctk _^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... The relation holds.

  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `memberAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-memberAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`:
   .... Let `typeIR [ _ ]` be `typeIR'`.
   .... If `nameIR` = `"next"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.

   .... Else if `nameIR` = `"last"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK /\ $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... If `p = LOCAL /\ $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)`:
     ...... The relation holds.
  ... If `$is_headerStackTypeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~base~>>)`:
   .... The relation holds.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `indexAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ]` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ] # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `sliceAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR-bitslice: `p`, `TC`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ] # ( _ _ )`

  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>> holds.
  ... The relation holds.

relation Expr_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `expressionIR # _`

