 .. Let `TYPE prefixedNameIR` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR # _`

  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
  ... If let `ENUM tid { _^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR`.

  ... Else if let `ENUM tid # _ { id~member~ = value~member~ ;^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Let `value'^?^` be `$assoc_<nameIR, value>(nameIR, (id~member~, value~member~)^{asterisk}^)`.
   .... Check that `value'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?value` be `value'^?^`.
   .... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR # value`.
. Let `( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `_`.
. If `expressionIR` has type `memberAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `memberAccessBaseIR . text` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Check that `text` is equal to `"size"`.
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "size" # ( typeIR~base~ _ )`

  ... Let `_ # ( typeIR _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
  ... Check that `typeIR` is equal to `typeIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
  ... Let `_ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `D n~size~`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `sliceAccessExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ] # _`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~base~ ==> STO~1~ value~base~`>>.
  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~hi~ ==> STO~2~ value~hi~`>>.
  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~2~ |- typedExpressionIR~lo~ ==> STO~3~ value~lo~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~3~` and `$bitacc_op(value~base~, value~hi~, value~lo~)`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `callExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`.
 .. If let `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... Group callExpressionIR-constructor: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # _`

   .... Let `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` be `$find_constructor_inst(IC, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^`.
   .... <<Constructor_inst, `p IC STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Let `STO~2~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, IC.PATH, object)`.
   .... Let `value~ref~` be `! IC.PATH`.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~ref~`.

 .. Else if let `routineTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... If `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
   .... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
   .... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( [ ] ) # _`

    ..... If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
     ...... Let `_ # ( typeIR~base~ _ )` be `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `STO'` and `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.

    ..... Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR` be `routineTargetIR`:
     ...... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `$find_typedef_inst(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)`.
     ...... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
     ...... Let `?typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
     ...... If `typeDefIR` has type `typeIR`:
      ....... Let `typeIR~base~` be `typeDefIR`.
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.

     ...... Else if `typeDefIR` has type `polyTypeDefIR`:
      ....... Let `typeIR~base~ < tid^{asterisk}^ , tid'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeDefIR`.
      ....... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
      ....... Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`.
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR' < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... If `routineTargetIR'` matches pattern `( % )`:
   .... Let `( routineTargetIR )` be `routineTargetIR'`.
   .... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `( routineTargetIR ) < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # expressionNoteIR`

    ..... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- routineTargetIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # _ ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.

. Else if `expressionIR` has type `parenthesizedExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `( typedExpressionIR )` be `expressionIR`.
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `( typedExpressionIR ) # _`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.

relation Exprs_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`

. If `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `STO'` and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~h~ :: typedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `typedExpressionIR~h~ :: typedExpressionIR~t~`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~h~ ==> STO~1~ value~h~`>>.
  ... <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> STO~2~ value~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~h~ :: value~t~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Argument_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `argumentIR`

. If `argumentIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`.
 .. Group typedExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `typedExpressionIR`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~0~ |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.
. If `argumentIR` matches pattern `% = %`:
 .. Let `nameIR = typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`.
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpressionIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`

  ... <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~0~ |- typedExpressionIR ==> STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.

relation Stmt_inst: `p'`, `IC'`, `STO'`, and `statementIR`

. If `statementIR` has type `emptyStatementIR`:
 .. Let `emptyStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group emptyStatementIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `emptyStatementIR`

  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO'`,
        * and the instantiated statement `emptyStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `assignmentStatementIR`:
 .. Let `assignmentStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group assignmentStatementIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `assignmentStatementIR`

  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO'`,
        * and the instantiated statement `assignmentStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `callStatementIR`:
 .. Let `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group callStatementIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `callStatementIR`

  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO'`,
        * and the instantiated statement `callStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `directApplicationStatementIR`:
 .. Let `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group directApplicationStatementIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, and `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;`

  ... Let `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` be `$find_constructor_inst(IC', prefixedNameIR, [ ])`.
  ... Check that `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?(_, constructor, _^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^`.
  ... <<Constructor_inst, `p' IC' STO' |- constructor < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~` be `$fresh_tid`.
  ... Let `tid` be `$flatten_prefixedNameIR(prefixedNameIR)`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `TID tid`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `$concat_text([tid, "_", tid~fresh~])`.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC'.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Let `routineTargetIR` be `` tid # ( typeIR CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `routineTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentListIR ) ;`.
  ... Let `blockStatementIR` be `{ [constantDeclarationIR, callStatementIR] }`.
  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO~2~`,
        * and the instantiated statement `blockStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `exitStatementIR`:
 .. Let `exitStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group exitStatementIR: `p`, `IC`, `STO`, and `exitStatementIR`

  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO'`,
        * and the instantiated statement `exitStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `conditionalStatementIR`:
 .. Let `conditionalStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group conditionalStatementIR: `p`, `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `conditionalStatementIR`

  ... If let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~then_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Result in 
          * the instantiation context `IC~1~`,
          * the updated store `STO~1~`,
          * and the instantiated statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then_inst~`.

  ... Else if let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~` be `conditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~then_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~then~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Let `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `statementIR~else_inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR~else~`, under cursor `p'`, instantiation context `IC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
   .... Result in 
          * the instantiation context `IC~2~`,
          * the updated store `STO~2~`,
          * and the instantiated statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then_inst~ ELSE statementIR~else_inst~`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `switchStatementIR`:
 .. Let `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR }` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group switchStatementIR: `p`, `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR }`

  ... <<SwitchCases_inst, `p' IC' STO' |- switchCaseListIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ switchCaseListIR~inst~`>>.
  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC~1~`,
        * the updated store `STO~1~`,
        * and the instantiated statement `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR ) { switchCaseListIR~inst~ }`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `LOCAL`.
. If `statementIR` has type `returnStatementIR`:
 .. Let `returnStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group returnStatementIR: `LOCAL`, `IC`, `STO`, and `returnStatementIR`

  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC'`,
        * the updated store `STO'`,
        * and the instantiated statement `returnStatementIR`.

. Else if `statementIR` has type `blockStatementIR`:
 .. Let `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }` be `statementIR`.
 .. Group blockStatementIR: `LOCAL`, `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }`

  ... <<Block_inst, `IC' STO' |- annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR } ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ _ { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`>>.
  ... Result in 
        * the instantiation context `IC~1~`,
        * the updated store `STO~1~`,
        * and the instantiated statement `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`.

relation BlockElementStmt_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `blockElementStatementIR`

. If `blockElementStatementIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `blockElementStatementIR`.
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `constantDeclarationIR`

  ... <<Decl_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- constantDeclarationIR ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
