. Else if `blockElementStatementIR` has type `statementIR`:
 .. Let `statementIR` be `blockElementStatementIR`.
 .. Group statementIR: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `statementIR`

  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR~inst~` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `statementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0'~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `?statementIR~inst~`.

relation BlockElementStmts_inst: `IC'`, `STO'`, and `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^`

. If `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^` matches pattern `[]`:
 .. Group nil: `IC`, `STO`, and `[ ]`

  ... Result in `IC'`, `STO'`, and `[ ]`.

. Else if let `blockElementStatementIR~h~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t~`

  ... <<BlockElementStmt_inst, `IC' STO' |- blockElementStatementIR~h~ ==> IC~1~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `blockElementStatementIR'^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
  ... Let `?blockElementStatementIR~h_inst~` be `blockElementStatementIR'^?^`.
  ... <<BlockElementStmts_inst, `IC~1~ STO~1~ |- blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ==> IC~2~ STO~2~ blockElementStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h_inst~ :: blockElementStatementIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.

relation Block_inst: `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }`

. Group : `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR }`

 .. Let `IC~1~` be `$enter_inst(IC~0~)`.
 .. <<BlockElementStmts_inst, `IC~1~ STO~0~ |- blockElementStatementListIR ==> IC~2~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementListIR~inst~`>>.
 .. Let `IC~3~` be `$exit_inst(IC~2~)`.
 .. Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~1~`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementListIR~inst~ }`.

relation Bind_method: `rdenv~0~` and `methodPrototypeIR`

. If let `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `methodPrototypeIR`:
 .. Group non-abstract: `rdenv~0~` and `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR ) ;`

  ... Let `rid` be `$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `rdenv~1~` be `$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
  ... Result in `rdenv~1~`.

. Else if let `annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR~ret~ nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `methodPrototypeIR`:
 .. Group abstract: `rdenv~0~` and `annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR~ret~ nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR ) ;`

  ... Let `rid` be `$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterIR^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be `$parameterIR(parameterIR)`
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `methodTypeIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) -> typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Let `routineTypeDefIR` be `methodTypeIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ >`.
  ... Let `rdenv~1~` be `$add_map<rid, routineTypeDefIR>(rdenv~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)`.
