relation Decl_inst: `cursor'`, `IC~0~`, `STO'`, and `declarationIR`

. If `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR: `cursor`, `IC~0~`, `STO`, and `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;`

  ... If `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, value)`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `?()`.

  ... Else if `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, value)`.
   .... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `?constantDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`:
 .. Let `annotationList typeIR prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) nameIR objectInitializerOptIR ;` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group instantiationIR: `cursor`, `IC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `annotationList typeIR prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) nameIR objectInitializerOptIR ;`

  ... If `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` be `$find_constructor_inst(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `$enter_path(IC~0~, nameIR)`.
   .... <<Constructor_inst, `GLOBAL IC~inner~ STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... If `object` has type `externObject`:
    ..... Let `EXTERN tid { tenv venv renv }` be `object`.
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `$empty_instantiationContext`[PATH = `IC~0~.PATH`][GLOBAL = `IC~0~.GLOBAL`].
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `$flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)`.
    ..... <<Decls_inst, `BLOCK IC~decl~ STO~1~ |- objectDeclarationListIR ==> IC~decl_post~ STO~2~ _^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `venv~merged~` be `$merge_venvs(venv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.VENV)`.
    ..... Let `renv~merged~` be `$merge_renv_with_extern(renv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.RENV)`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid { tenv venv~merged~ renv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and `?()`.
   .... If `$is_extern_object(object)`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `?()`.

  ... Else if `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` be `$find_constructor_inst(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^` matches pattern `(_)`.
   .... Let `?(_, constructor, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructor, id*)^?^`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `$enter_path(IC~0~, nameIR)`.
   .... <<Constructor_inst, `cursor' IC~inner~ STO' |- constructor < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) ==> STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... If `object` has type `externObject`:
    ..... Let `EXTERN tid { tenv venv renv }` be `object`.
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `$empty_instantiationContext`[PATH = `IC~0~.PATH`][GLOBAL = `IC~0~.GLOBAL`].
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `$flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)`.
    ..... <<Decls_inst, `BLOCK IC~decl~ STO~1~ |- objectDeclarationListIR ==> IC~decl_post~ STO~2~ _^{asterisk}^`>>.
    ..... Let `venv~merged~` be `$merge_venvs(venv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.VENV)`.
    ..... Let `renv~merged~` be `$merge_renv_with_extern(renv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.RENV)`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid { tenv venv~merged~ renv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and `?constantDeclarationIR`.
   .... If `$is_extern_object(object)`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH ++ [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `$add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_value_inst(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `?constantDeclarationIR`.

. Else if `declarationIR` has type `functionDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `annotationList typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group functionDeclarationIR: `p`, `IC~0~`, `STO`, and `annotationList typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`

  ... Let `rid` be `$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)`.
  ... Let `function` be `FUNCTION < typeParameterListIR ++ typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_routine_overload_inst(cursor', IC~0~, rid, function)`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `?()`.

. Else if `declarationIR` has type `actionDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group actionDeclarationIR: `p`, `IC~0~`, `STO`, and `annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`

  ... Let `rid` be `$rid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)`.
  ... Let `function` be `ACTION ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_routine_non_overload_inst(cursor', IC~0~, rid, function)`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `?()`.
. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. If `declarationIR` has type `errorDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `ERROR { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group errorDeclarationIR: `GLOBAL`, `IC~0~`, `STO`, and `ERROR { nameIR }`

  ... Let `nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR~error~` be `$concat_text(["error.", nameIR])`
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `value~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~error~` be `ERROR . nameIR`
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `$add_values_inst(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^, value~error~^{asterisk}^)`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `?()`.

. Else if `declarationIR` has type `matchKindDeclarationIR`:
 .. Let `MATCH_KIND { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`.
 .. Group matchKindDeclarationIR: `GLOBAL`, `IC~0~`, `STO`, and `MATCH_KIND { nameIR }`

  ... Let `value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~match_kind~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~match_kind~` be `MATCH_KIND . nameIR`
--
